1
00:00:02,620 --> 00:00:04,360
-我什么都没说 -别说话了
- I didn't say anything. - Stop talking.

2
00:00:04,560 --> 00:00:05,300
你这也是在说话
That's talking.

3
00:00:05,620 --> 00:00:06,720
你觉得她睡着了吗
You think she's asleep yet?

4
00:00:06,760 --> 00:00:08,120
我和你一样都在门外啊
I'm on the same side of the door as you are.

5
00:00:08,140 --> 00:00:09,300
-别说话了 -小卡
- Stop talking. - Cam.

6
00:00:09,620 --> 00:00:11,320
莉莉今天掉了第一颗牙
Lily lost her first tooth today.

7
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:14,100
她现在非常期待牙仙子的到访
And she's very excited about the visit from the tooth fairy.

8
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:16,449
我第一次有牙齿松动时
When I have my first loose tooth,

9
00:00:16,449 --> 00:00:18,917
我妈将绳子一端系在那颗牙上
my mom tied one end of the string to it,

10
00:00:19,080 --> 00:00:20,900
另一端系在奶牛的尾巴上
the other to the tail of a cow

11
00:00:21,020 --> 00:00:22,480
用12号猎枪开了一枪
fired off a 12-gauge shotgun,

12
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:24,180
奶牛跑出了房间
and the cow went running out of the room.

13
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:25,160
本故事纯属虚构
That never happened.

14
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:27,160
你去看看我卧室里的奶牛型墙洞再说
Tell that to the cow-shaped hole in my bedroom wall.

15
00:00:36,619 --> 00:00:37,169
抓住了
Gotcha!

16
00:00:38,260 --> 00:00:39,380
你们跑我房里来干嘛
what are you doing here?

17
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:41,040
你们又不是牙仙子
You're not the tooth fairy.

18
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:44,080
不 我们就是想来看看她来了没
N-no. But we just wanted to see if she'd come yet.

19
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:46,780
没呢 看来她真的一点都不着急
No. She sure is taking her sweet time.

20
00:00:46,980 --> 00:00:48,620
-也许你该继续睡觉 亲爱的 -对
- Maybe you should just go back to sleep, sweetie. - Yeah.

21
00:00:48,620 --> 00:00:50,467
因为可能还要再等一会儿
'cause it could take a while.

22
00:00:51,640 --> 00:00:53,680
我时间多的是
I've got nowhere to be.

23
00:01:06,980 --> 00:01:08,240
妈 我今天不能迟到
Mom, I can't be late today.

24
00:01:08,420 --> 00:01:09,880
桑杰·帕特尔和我要解剖一头猪
Sanjay Patel and I are dissecting a pig.

25
00:01:09,940 --> 00:01:11,820
你这辈子所谓的约会真可悲啊
So sad what passes for a date in your life.

26
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:14,480
-海莉 -他老是让我拿工具给他
- Haley. - He keeps asking me to hand him all of the instruments.

27
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:16,220
他想让我扮演护士的角色
He wants me to act like a nurse.

28
00:01:16,340 --> 00:01:18,180
那听起来像是海莉的约会
Now it sounds like a date in Haley's life.

29
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:19,920
在你说"不行"之前
Okay, before you say no...

30
00:01:20,100 --> 00:01:21,400
-不行 -你连看都没看呢
- No. - You haven't even seen it yet.

31
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:22,580
我还是要说不行
Mm, I'm sticking with "No."

32
00:01:22,580 --> 00:01:23,740
这是为卢克的职业日准备的
It's for Luke's Career Day.

33
00:01:23,760 --> 00:01:24,960
我想我可以让孩子们尝试
I thought I'd offer the kids a chance

34
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:26,180
把脸放在我的身体上
to put their face on my body.

35
00:01:26,784 --> 00:01:27,888
我也刚意识到很变态
I just heard it, too.

36
00:01:28,700 --> 00:01:29,980
你们怎么从来没办过职业日
How come you guys never had a Career Day?

37
00:01:30,266 --> 00:01:31,621
-经费削减 -东北大风暴停课
- Cutbacks. - Nor'easter.

38
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:35,880
今天我要讲述我的一生挚爱
Today I get to talk about the love of my life...

39
00:01:36,760 --> 00:01:37,820
住宅房地产
residential real estate.

40
00:01:38,040 --> 00:01:39,080
他真是意识不到自己在说什么
He really doesn't hear it.

41
00:01:39,080 --> 00:01:40,174
我要让卢克感到骄傲
I wanna make Luke proud.

42
00:01:40,174 --> 00:01:41,780
我要成为他的英雄
I wanna be his hero like my dad was

43
00:01:41,780 --> 00:01:42,780
就像以前我父亲向我的同学们
when he talked to my class

44
00:01:42,780 --> 00:01:44,000
讲述开杂货店的故事时那样
about running a grocery store.

45
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:46,940
他拿着两把带皮套的价格标枪进屋
He came in with two price guns in holsters

46
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:48,700
在我们的老师还没反应过来时
and marked our teacher at $1.29

47
00:01:48,700 --> 00:01:49,960
给她打了个1.29刀的标签
before she knew what hit her.

48
00:01:50,120 --> 00:01:52,040
我敢说那肯定"很好笑"
I bet that produced a lot of laughs.

49
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:52,840
克莱尔 拜托
Claire, please.

50
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:55,780
奥利维亚·伯曼的妈妈
And Olivia Berman's mom

51
00:01:55,780 --> 00:01:57,760
在图书馆的珍本书部工作
works in the rare books department at the library.

52
00:01:58,080 --> 00:01:59,600
真希望我有机会去向她讨教讨教
Hope I get a chance to pick that brain.

53
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:01,700
看来你们的职业日已经排得满满当当了
Looks like you got quite the Career Day lineup.

54
00:02:02,060 --> 00:02:04,600
我猜他们已经邀请到搞衣柜的人了吧
So I guess they already got a closet guy coming in, huh?

55
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:06,280
没有 我以为你不想参加
No. I didn't think you'd wanna do it.

56
00:02:06,280 --> 00:02:08,360
我不想 但是 我只是为孩子们感到遗憾
I don't, but you know, I just feel bad for the kids.

57
00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:10,620
衣柜这行有很多有趣的事情
A lot of interesting stories in the closet biz.

58
00:02:10,620 --> 00:02:12,600
你怎么从来没跟我们讲过
Oh. Why have you never told us any?

59
00:02:12,820 --> 00:02:15,760
好吧 比如曾经有个家伙
Okay. Well, for example, there was this guy...

60
00:02:16,557 --> 00:02:18,820
-有100多顶帽子 -然后呢
- must have had over a hundred hats... - Yes?

61
00:02:18,820 --> 00:02:20,240
我们得想办法把那些帽子都放进衣柜里
And we had to fit them in the closet.

62
00:02:21,580 --> 00:02:21,980
然后呢
Okay?

63
00:02:23,340 --> 00:02:24,280
我们做到了
And we did.

64
00:02:25,980 --> 00:02:28,360
好吧 也许这不是世上最刺激的职业
All right. Maybe it's not the most exciting career in the world,

65
00:02:28,360 --> 00:02:29,200
但这真的很挣钱
but it pays the bills.

66
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:30,500
没人嫌弃
No one is complaining.

67
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:32,760
要问我想不想干别的事情 想啊
Were there other things I'd rather do? Yes.

68
00:02:32,760 --> 00:02:34,840
-但我得维持生计 -别的什么事情
- But I had to make ends meet. - What other things?

69
00:02:34,840 --> 00:02:36,138
我一直想写惊悚小说
Well, I always wanted to write thrillers.

70
00:02:36,580 --> 00:02:38,900
-比如那个帽子的故事吗 -间谍惊悚小说
- Like that hat story? - Spy thrillers.

71
00:02:39,080 --> 00:02:40,600
我已经仔细考虑过主角的身份了
I've been kicking around this character,

72
00:02:40,820 --> 00:02:42,720
中情局探员查克·斯通 他毫不在意
CIA agent Chuck Stone, who doesn't care

73
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:45,080
自己的古怪行为会惹恼阿灵顿的高层们
how much his antics annoy the brass in Arlington.

74
00:02:45,300 --> 00:02:46,440
你为什么不写写看
Why didn't you ever try it?

75
00:02:46,440 --> 00:02:48,080
我一直忙于工作和家庭
I was busy with work and family.

76
00:02:48,080 --> 00:02:50,080
我本打算离婚后开始写
I was gonna start writing after my divorce,

77
00:02:50,080 --> 00:02:52,320
但是被生活琐事妨碍了
But you know... life got in the way.

78
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:54,900
你说生活琐事的时候为什么指着我
Why do you point at me when you say "Life"?

79
00:02:55,040 --> 00:02:55,680
我是生活琐事吗
Am I "Life"?

80
00:02:55,680 --> 00:02:56,957
我是说你让我忙碌了起来
I meant you keep my busy.

81
00:02:56,957 --> 00:02:58,760
你周日睡了3个小时午觉
You had a 3-hour nap on Sunday.

82
00:02:58,760 --> 00:03:00,240
-我很累 -为什么累
- I was tired. From what?

83
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:02,190
因为周六睡了两个小时午觉吗
Your 2-hour nap on Saturday?

84
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:04,840
杰 我跟你在一起5年了
Jay, I've been with you for five years,

85
00:03:04,840 --> 00:03:07,280
可从没听你说过什么写书的事
and I've never heard you mention anything about writing.

86
00:03:07,380 --> 00:03:09,040
我买了台打字机
Hey. I bought a typewriter.

87
00:03:09,220 --> 00:03:10,700
打字机
A typewriter?

88
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:13,240
你的签售会安排在什么时候
When is your book signing?

89
00:03:15,400 --> 00:03:16,440
我的小说人物非常可怕
It's a hell of a character.

90
00:03:16,880 --> 00:03:18,020
他们教他如何杀人
They taught him how to kill,

91
00:03:18,020 --> 00:03:19,580
但他从没学过如何去爱
but he never learned to love!

92
00:03:20,489 --> 00:03:22,106
不不不 等等 等等
No, no, no, no, no. Wait, wait. Okay.

93
00:03:22,106 --> 00:03:24,409
爸爸 爸爸 牙仙子来过了
Daddies! Daddies! The tooth fairy came.

94
00:03:24,409 --> 00:03:28,380
-什么 不是吧 -真叫人激动
- What? No way! - Oh, that's so exciting!

95
00:03:28,380 --> 00:03:29,540
她给你带了什么
What'd she bring you?

96
00:03:32,160 --> 00:03:34,660
仙尘啊 真不错
Oh! Fairy dust. Nice touch.

97
00:03:34,660 --> 00:03:36,053
天呐 太多了
Oh, my gosh, it's a lot.

98
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:37,500
还有贴纸
Some stickers...

99
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:40,080
一把牙刷
A toothbrush...

100
00:03:42,101 --> 00:03:43,632
还有一张百元大钞
And a hundred dollar bill!

101
00:03:43,632 --> 00:03:45,300
-什么 -快瞧瞧
- What? Okay. - Look at that.

102
00:03:45,820 --> 00:03:47,760
我爱牙仙子
I love the tooth fairy.

103
00:03:47,920 --> 00:03:49,720
牙仙子给我们家女儿100美元呢
The tooth fairy gave our daughter $100.

104
00:03:50,700 --> 00:03:54,120
她不知道一颗牙的市场价格顶多5美元吗
Does she not know that the going rate for a tooth is $5 at the most?

105
00:03:54,160 --> 00:03:56,180
显然 牙仙子搞错了
Well, obviously, the tooth fairy made a mistake.

106
00:03:56,406 --> 00:03:57,343
可能是因为牙仙子
Maybe it's 'cause the tooth fairy

107
00:03:57,343 --> 00:03:59,040
昨晚喝了太多夏敦埃酒
had a little too much chardonnay last night.

108
00:03:59,040 --> 00:04:00,760
我觉得牙仙子能扛得住夏敦埃酒
I think the tooth fairy can handle the chardonnay.

109
00:04:00,920 --> 00:04:02,060
但她恐怕无法接受
What I don't think she can handle

110
00:04:02,060 --> 00:04:04,060
批评别人在漆黑的夜里
is criticizing someone who made an honest mistake

111
00:04:04,060 --> 00:04:04,920
所犯下的无心之过
in the dark of the night.

112
00:04:05,100 --> 00:04:06,600
我要把它放进我的小手包里
I'm gonna put this in my clutch.

113
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:09,680
我等不及要告诉学校里的每个人了
I can't wait to tell everyone at school!

114
00:04:11,260 --> 00:04:13,540
听着 我们做父母的可不能冒充牙仙
Okay, we cannot be the parents of a 6-year-old

115
00:04:13,540 --> 00:04:15,540
给6岁的女儿一张百元大钞
who gets $100 from the tooth fairy.

116
00:04:15,540 --> 00:04:18,260
我们的孩子才6岁就有手包已经够离谱了
It's bad enough we're the parents of a 6-year-old with a clutch.

117
00:04:18,260 --> 00:04:21,320
那个包从早到晚都可以用
You know, that bag transitions from day to night seamlessly,

118
00:04:21,320 --> 00:04:23,720
而且我不用再在口袋里装蜡笔了
and I no longer have to carry crayons in my front pocket.

119
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:25,040
不要再争这个了
Can't have this argument again!

120
00:04:25,880 --> 00:04:27,340
安医生 谢谢你
Thank you, Dr. Ann,

121
00:04:27,340 --> 00:04:29,800
向我们展示了真实的心理辅导
for showing us how exciting and surprising

122
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:31,846
多么令人激动和惊喜
a real live therapy session can be.

123
00:04:32,060 --> 00:04:33,480
我会收好这张名片的
I will hold on to this card.

124
00:04:34,380 --> 00:04:37,120
接下来 有请卢克的爸爸 邓菲先生
Next up, we have Luke's dad, Mr. Dunphy.

125
00:04:37,320 --> 00:04:39,260
谢谢
Hey. Thank you.

126
00:04:40,900 --> 00:04:41,840
你们猜怎么着
Guess what?

127
00:04:41,840 --> 00:04:43,740
你不在家的时候我去过你家
I've been in your house when you weren't home.

128
00:04:44,020 --> 00:04:46,600
还有你家 你家也去过
And yours. And yours.

129
00:04:47,220 --> 00:04:50,220
不 我不是小偷 我是房地产经纪人
No, I'm not a burglar. I'm a realtor.

130
00:04:50,433 --> 00:04:52,620
抱歉我迟到了
Ho! Hey, sorry I'm late!

131
00:04:52,620 --> 00:04:54,260
我刚刚又卖出去一座豪宅
I just sold another mansion.

132
00:04:55,135 --> 00:04:56,151
你好吗 亲爱的
How you doin', honey?

133
00:04:56,680 --> 00:04:58,100
历史充满了激烈的竞争
History is full of great rivalries--

134
00:04:58,140 --> 00:05:00,080
雅典与斯巴达 凯瑞甘与哈丁
Athens and Sparta, Kerrigan and Harding,

135
00:05:00,660 --> 00:05:02,380
菲尔·邓菲和格尔·索普
Phil Dunphy and Gil Thorpe.

136
00:05:02,840 --> 00:05:05,300
现在这种局面 他是汤娅 我是南希
In this scenario, he's the Tonya, I'm the Nancy.

137
00:05:06,100 --> 00:05:07,120
注意了 孩子们
Pay attention, kids.

138
00:05:07,320 --> 00:05:10,680
即将演讲的是镇上排名第4的地产经纪人
You're about to hear from the number four realtor in town.

139
00:05:12,280 --> 00:05:15,640
无论如何 我不打算做无聊的演讲
Anyway, uh, I'm not gonna bore you guys with a lecture.

140
00:05:15,640 --> 00:05:17,580
相反 我想让你们看看
Instead, I'd like you to watch

141
00:05:17,580 --> 00:05:19,120
我和一个年轻人之间的对话
as I converse with a young man

142
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:22,160
他正在思考自己的人生目标
who's wondering what to do with his life.

143
00:05:22,840 --> 00:05:23,620
孩子你好
Hey, kid.

144
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:26,460
孩子 看这里 看这里
Hey, kid, up here! Up here!

145
00:05:27,540 --> 00:05:29,260
老兄 什么事
Yo, dude! Whassup?

146
00:05:29,260 --> 00:05:30,420
我来告诉你什么事
I'll tell you what's up.

147
00:05:30,760 --> 00:05:32,300
我想帮助你
I'm interested in helping you

148
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:34,280
给你讲讲在房地产界打拼的事情
by telling you all about a career in real estate.

149
00:05:34,280 --> 00:05:37,320
房地产 不就是买房子和卖房子吗
Real estate? Isn't that just buying and selling houses?

150
00:05:37,320 --> 00:05:39,660
我没空搞那个 太没用了
I don't have time for that. Epic fail.

151
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:42,700
看来我们得从头讲起了
Sounds like we need to start at the beginning.

152
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:44,520
你看 房地产这行的重点就是人
You see, real estate is about people.

153
00:05:47,980 --> 00:05:48,500
人
People?

154
00:05:48,980 --> 00:05:51,140
你说得太对了菲尔 我们这份工作
Couldn't agree more, Phil. Best part of our job

155
00:05:51,140 --> 00:05:52,660
最大的妙处就是让对的人住进对的家
is putting the right person in the right home.

156
00:05:52,660 --> 00:05:54,220
-格尔 -实际上 就在上周
- Gil... - Matter of fact, last week,

157
00:05:54,220 --> 00:05:55,920
我让一对"西班牙"夫妇住进了
I put a "Spanish" Couple into

158
00:05:55,920 --> 00:05:56,980
-西班牙式的房子 -格尔
- a Spanish home. - Gil.

159
00:05:56,980 --> 00:05:59,200
一个没有房子的世界 那真是太疯狂了
A world without houses? That's cray cray.

160
00:05:59,200 --> 00:05:59,949
好的 好的
Okay. Okay.

161
00:05:59,949 --> 00:06:01,820
菲尔对不起 我不是故意搞砸你的表演
Phil, I'm sorry. I didn't mean to screw up your little show.

162
00:06:01,820 --> 00:06:03,300
我知道这种表演把握好时间最重要
I know timing is critical on these things.

163
00:06:03,583 --> 00:06:05,400
-拜托格尔 -相信我 我最不想
- Gil, please. - Believe me, the last thing I want to do is...

164
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:08,520
7频道天气预报员的房子是你卖给他的吗
You sold a house to the channel 7 weatherman?

165
00:06:08,780 --> 00:06:09,680
不 不是
No. No.

166
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:11,680
但科比·布莱恩特有套房子是我卖给他的
But I did sell one to Kobe Bryant.

167
00:06:11,780 --> 00:06:14,460
什么 他不是在跟你说话 是跟我
What?! Guess what? He's not talking to you. He's talking to me.

168
00:06:14,460 --> 00:06:16,520
其实我有个很好笑的故事要讲
And I have a very funny story, actually.

169
00:06:16,520 --> 00:06:19,120
-有个人走进...不 -太好笑了
- A guy walks into... No. - That's hilarious.

170
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:20,900
不 我还没讲呢
No! I haven't told it!

171
00:06:21,400 --> 00:06:23,120
好吧 对了
Okay, um... Oh!

172
00:06:24,580 --> 00:06:26,320
好球 你说得对
Great throw. You were right.

173
00:06:26,320 --> 00:06:28,342
-确实该看我的了 -就看你的了
- It is in my court. - Ball's in your court!

174
00:06:28,342 --> 00:06:31,142
但你们猜怎么着 其实一直都是我
But guess what-- it was me the whole time.

175
00:06:33,420 --> 00:06:33,860
怎样
What?!

176
00:06:34,407 --> 00:06:36,060
快点孩子们 快点
Come on, kids, come on.

177
00:06:36,060 --> 00:06:39,220
鼓起掌来 鼓起来 他尽力了
Give it up! Give it up! He tried.

178
00:06:39,460 --> 00:06:41,280
我想我们都明白你的意思 菲尔
I think we all know what you were going for, Phil.

179
00:06:41,640 --> 00:06:44,080
不过我看到有几个孩子饿了
But I'm lookin' out here, and I'm seeing some hungry kids.

180
00:06:44,140 --> 00:06:46,120
我说对了没 所以我才买了这么多的
Am I right? That's why I brought plenty of...

181
00:06:46,120 --> 00:06:47,360
格尔腌黄瓜
Gil pickles!

182
00:06:47,960 --> 00:06:48,820
谁想来个格尔腌黄瓜
Who wants a Gil pickle?

183
00:06:48,820 --> 00:06:49,760
来吧 我看都有谁
Come on. Let me see 'em.

184
00:06:49,760 --> 00:06:51,060
好的 来吧 来拿吧
All right. Come on. Grab one.

185
00:06:51,500 --> 00:06:52,400
格尔腌黄瓜
Gil pickles.

186
00:06:53,880 --> 00:06:54,360
太有才了
Genius.

187
00:06:54,609 --> 00:06:57,220
比我的菲尔枕套强多了
So much better than my Phil-low cases.

188
00:06:57,740 --> 00:06:58,740
克莱尔都不喜欢
Claire wasn't a fan.

189
00:06:59,160 --> 00:07:01,060
床上有一个他已经足够了
One of him in bed is more than enough.

190
00:07:02,001 --> 00:07:03,378
听到了吗 女士们
Do you hear that, ladies?

191
00:07:08,160 --> 00:07:09,480
好了 点击"发送"键
All right. Just hit "Send."

192
00:07:10,280 --> 00:07:11,720
你刚刚卖出了一幢房子
Hey! You just sold a house!

193
00:07:12,160 --> 00:07:14,700
而那就是你余生要追求的高目标
And you're gonna be chasing that high for the rest of your life.

194
00:07:14,700 --> 00:07:16,220
大家给她鼓鼓掌吧
Give her a round of applause, everybody.

195
00:07:16,240 --> 00:07:17,100
她刚刚卖出了一幢房子
She just sold a house.

196
00:07:18,500 --> 00:07:20,420
孩子们 感谢你们今天请我来
I wanna thank you kids for having me here today.

197
00:07:20,480 --> 00:07:22,620
请记住房地产这一行的三大准则
And remember the three rules of real estate--

198
00:07:23,080 --> 00:07:24,380
索普 索普 索普
Thorpe, Thorpe, Thorpe!

199
00:07:25,180 --> 00:07:26,820
谢谢你 索普先生
Thank you, Mr. Thorpe.

200
00:07:27,140 --> 00:07:29,420
看来我们还剩下一些时间
It turns out we have a little extra time.

201
00:07:29,420 --> 00:07:30,900
-邓菲太太 -怎么了
- Uh, Mrs. Dunphy? - Yes?

202
00:07:30,900 --> 00:07:32,940
同学们一定想听听你的工作
I'm sure the class would love to hear from you.

203
00:07:33,180 --> 00:07:34,900
不 我只是过来给我老公帮忙的
Oh, no. I just came in to help my husband.

204
00:07:34,900 --> 00:07:36,100
我是个全职主妇
I'm a... I'm a stay-at-home mom.

205
00:07:36,100 --> 00:07:38,720
我知道 那也是个很重要的职业
I know. And that's a very important job.

206
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:40,691
没错 好吧
It is. Uh, yeah.

207
00:07:40,691 --> 00:07:42,733
我可以 我可以讲一讲
I can--I can do this for a minute.

208
00:07:42,986 --> 00:07:44,684
全职主妇
Um, stay-at-home mom.

209
00:07:44,947 --> 00:07:47,060
那就意味着 我实际上
Uh, what that means is I actually have

210
00:07:47,060 --> 00:07:48,180
要做好几项不同的工作
a whole bunch of different jobs.

211
00:07:48,320 --> 00:07:50,880
我既是司机 也是厨师
I am a chauffeur, a chef,

212
00:07:51,112 --> 00:07:52,521
还是管家
Uh, a house manager,

213
00:07:52,780 --> 00:07:55,020
-护士 -这是你小时候的理想吗
- A nurse. - Is it what you always wanted to do?

214
00:07:55,100 --> 00:07:56,940
不 不算吧
No. Not exactly.

215
00:07:56,940 --> 00:07:59,900
我上过大学 学的是市场营销
Uh, I went to college, uh, to study marketing

216
00:07:59,900 --> 00:08:02,460
还在一家大型酒店企业工作过
and worked at one of those big hotel companies.

217
00:08:02,500 --> 00:08:03,820
但自从我有了孩子
But when my kids came along,

218
00:08:03,880 --> 00:08:05,860
我就想在家照顾他们
I just wanted to be there.

219
00:08:05,860 --> 00:08:08,900
给他们擦鼻涕 给他们换尿布
You know, wipe their noses and change their diapers

220
00:08:08,900 --> 00:08:10,300
夜里给他们盖好被子
And tuck 'em in at night.

221
00:08:10,300 --> 00:08:10,840
妈妈
Mom!

222
00:08:11,640 --> 00:08:13,380
郑重声明 我擦什么都是自己擦的
For the record, I do all my own wiping.

223
00:08:13,740 --> 00:08:15,100
那你为什么不重返职场呢
So why haven't you gone back to work?

224
00:08:15,180 --> 00:08:18,040
我最近做了很多事 我整修了一幢房子
I've done a few things lately. I just redid a house,

225
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:20,740
去年还参选了市政议员
and I ran for city council last year.

226
00:08:20,780 --> 00:08:21,700
你现在是市政议员吗
You're on the city council?

227
00:08:21,700 --> 00:08:23,500
不 我没当上
No. I-I didn't win.

228
00:08:23,500 --> 00:08:24,980
-你输了 -不是说了"没当上"吗
- You lost? - That's what "Didn't win" means.

229
00:08:26,040 --> 00:08:27,860
我本来想等孩子们长大些
I... I thought I would be going back to work

230
00:08:27,860 --> 00:08:28,880
就回去工作
when the kids got older,

231
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:31,280
不过 这事没有你们想的那么简单
But it--it's not as easy as you might think.

232
00:08:31,640 --> 00:08:33,260
要知道 一个年近40的女人
You know, people aren't exactly lining up

233
00:08:33,260 --> 00:08:34,500
在职场上并不抢手
to hire a woman who's almost 40

234
00:08:34,500 --> 00:08:36,420
何况我都15年没有工作了
and has been out of the job market for 15 years.

235
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:37,800
我记得你已经42岁了
I thought you were 42.

236
00:08:37,960 --> 00:08:39,220
42和40很接近 卢克
That's almost 40, Luke.

237
00:08:39,220 --> 00:08:40,960
我4岁时我妈妈就回去工作了
My mom went back to work when I was 4.

238
00:08:41,300 --> 00:08:43,260
所以你家才没有人教你不要打断别人说话
Oh, so there was no one at home to teach you not to interrupt?

239
00:08:43,260 --> 00:08:44,760
好了 好了
Okay. Hey, hey, hey!

240
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:45,960
我来告诉你们吧
Let me tell you something.

241
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:48,040
全职妈妈们都是英雄
Stay-at-home moms are heroes.

242
00:08:48,180 --> 00:08:49,940
-没错 -她们是这个国家的栋梁
- Yeah. - They're the backbone of this country.

243
00:08:50,080 --> 00:08:50,520
谢了 格尔
Thanks, Gil.

244
00:08:50,760 --> 00:08:51,860
如果非要我做那样的工作
I mean, if I had to do that job,

245
00:08:51,860 --> 00:08:54,060
我大概早把自己喝死了 真的
I'd probably drink myself to death, honestly.

246
00:08:54,460 --> 00:08:56,020
好了 我们给她一些掌声吧
All right, let's give her a round of applause, everybody.

247
00:08:56,040 --> 00:08:56,500
来嘛
Come on.

248
00:08:57,520 --> 00:08:59,080
来嘛 把手拍响点儿 让我听见
Oh, come on, you can do better than that. Let me hear ya!

249
00:08:59,800 --> 00:09:01,200
很好 很好
All right! All right!

250
00:09:01,260 --> 00:09:02,820
好了 下课了 都走吧
All right, class dismissed. Get out of here!

251
00:09:02,860 --> 00:09:03,180
不
No!

252
00:09:04,300 --> 00:09:05,420
不 不 不
No, no, no.

253
00:09:05,420 --> 00:09:07,640
还有 同学们 还有3个小时才结束
We have... Guys, we have three more hours.

254
00:09:10,700 --> 00:09:12,480
-给 -我的旧打字机
- Here. - My old typewriter.

255
00:09:12,640 --> 00:09:14,600
你不是说你想写作吗 写吧
You said you want to write. Write.

256
00:09:14,780 --> 00:09:16,920
现在吗 我今天很忙
Now? I've got a busy day.

257
00:09:17,020 --> 00:09:17,900
我已经给你办公室打过电话了
I already called your office

258
00:09:17,900 --> 00:09:19,440
告诉他们 你今天不会去公司
And told them that you can't come in

259
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:20,920
乱晃上20分钟
to walk around for 20 minutes

260
00:09:20,920 --> 00:09:23,420
跟每个人说 "怎么样 小子"
saying to everyone, "What's up, sport?"

261
00:09:23,480 --> 00:09:25,020
我明白 你暗含的意思是
I know this is your subtle little way

262
00:09:25,020 --> 00:09:26,740
你觉得我写不出东西
of saying you don't think I can do it.

263
00:09:26,800 --> 00:09:29,180
不 我是让生活琐事为你让路
No. It's life getting out of the way.

264
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:31,440
好吧 我这就接受你的小小挑战
Fine. I'm gonna take you up on your little challenge,

265
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:32,280
不过你要知道
but you should know this--

266
00:09:32,520 --> 00:09:34,340
等你人老珠黄那天 你这种行为
this behavior of yours is not gonna fly

267
00:09:34,340 --> 00:09:35,140
就不会得逞了
when you lose your looks.

268
00:09:36,880 --> 00:09:41,060
到那时你都死好久了
You're gonna be long gone by then.

269
00:09:46,215 --> 00:09:47,337
-邓菲 -有事吗
- Dunphy. - Yeah? Oh.

270
00:09:47,560 --> 00:09:49,580
-你还好吗 -我很好 我很好
- You okay? - I'm fine. I'm fine.

271
00:09:49,580 --> 00:09:51,860
别因为那个自作聪明的小屁孩烦心
Don't let that little smart-ass bother you, all right.

272
00:09:51,860 --> 00:09:53,860
你见过她妈妈没有 人老珠黄憔悴损
Have you seen her mother? Does not age well.

273
00:09:54,176 --> 00:09:57,220
谢谢你帮我解围
well, um, thanks for rescuing me in there.

274
00:09:57,220 --> 00:09:58,340
顺便帮我跟菲尔说声抱歉吧
And tell Phil I'm sorry

275
00:09:58,340 --> 00:09:59,300
我刚刚可能让他难堪了
if I threw him off in there.

276
00:09:59,360 --> 00:10:01,520
我真是应该学着管好自己的大嘴巴
I probably should learn just to keep my big blowhole shut.

277
00:10:01,800 --> 00:10:04,140
其实那已经比他排练时好很多了
Actually, it went a little better than it did in rehearsal,

278
00:10:04,140 --> 00:10:05,120
说真的
to be honest.

279
00:10:05,120 --> 00:10:06,980
-不过我会向他转达 -好
- But I will tell him what you said. - All right.

280
00:10:07,080 --> 00:10:08,840
你刚才略为抓狂的表现让我想起些事情
You know, your little meltdown in there got me thinking.

281
00:10:09,560 --> 00:10:11,760
我正在开发一处零售和办公区
I'm building a retail office development,

282
00:10:11,800 --> 00:10:12,720
因此我需要有人
and I could use a liaison

283
00:10:12,720 --> 00:10:13,860
负责联络规划委员会
to work with the planning commission.

284
00:10:15,100 --> 00:10:16,460
你是要雇用我吗
Are you offering me a job?

285
00:10:16,460 --> 00:10:18,060
是的 你认识市政厅的人
Well, yeah. You know people in city hall,

286
00:10:18,060 --> 00:10:19,740
而且你炒房也炒得很不错
and you did a hell of a job on that flip.

287
00:10:20,040 --> 00:10:21,660
为了你和你家人的安全
And for the safety of you and your family,

288
00:10:21,660 --> 00:10:22,860
我得让你从家里出来
I gotta get you out of that house.

289
00:10:22,860 --> 00:10:24,880
可你和菲尔是竞争对手
But you and Phil are competitors. It--

290
00:10:24,880 --> 00:10:25,640
这事没竞争
Not on this.

291
00:10:26,020 --> 00:10:28,040
听我说 这事要成了 对大家都好
Look, if this works out, everybody's gonna win...

292
00:10:28,380 --> 00:10:30,460
除了我们要赶走的那家热带鱼店
Except for that tropical fish store we're booting out of there.

293
00:10:30,620 --> 00:10:32,180
我对此一点罪恶感都没有
I don't feel bad about that at all.

294
00:10:32,180 --> 00:10:34,340
你能让我回去想几天吗
Can I take a couple of days to think about it?

295
00:10:34,620 --> 00:10:36,240
-没问题 慢慢想 不着急 -好
- Yeah. Yeah. Take your time. No pressure. - Okay.

296
00:10:36,240 --> 00:10:37,940
你想好了 就给我个电话
And when you're ready, just give me a call.

297
00:10:38,100 --> 00:10:39,180
-好的 -木棒上有我电话
- Okay. - Number's on the stick.

298
00:10:39,240 --> 00:10:41,840
好的 格尔腌黄瓜
Great. Oh, yeah. Okay. Gil pickle.

299
00:10:42,020 --> 00:10:43,340
回见 索普 索普 索普
See ya! Thorpe! Thorpe! Thorpe!

300
00:10:43,400 --> 00:10:44,700
索普 索普 索普
Thorpe. Thorpe. Thorpe.

301
00:10:47,380 --> 00:10:49,620
猜我在信箱里发现了什么
Look what just came in the mail--

302
00:10:49,720 --> 00:10:51,960
莉莉 是寄给你的信
A letter addressed to you, Lily.

303
00:10:52,515 --> 00:10:54,106
是吗 很少有人寄信给我
Really? I don't get much mail.

304
00:10:54,106 --> 00:10:55,185
我们看看
Oh, let's see here.

305
00:10:55,709 --> 00:10:57,372
是牙仙子寄来的
Uh, yeah. Oh, the tooth fairy.

306
00:10:57,619 --> 00:11:02,240
牙达科他州 牙市 牙仙子街1号
"1 Tooth Fairy Lane. Tooth City, Tooth Dakota."

307
00:11:03,031 --> 00:11:05,249
希望她又送我100美元
I hope it's another $100.

308
00:11:05,249 --> 00:11:06,420
我们看看是什么
Ooh! Well, lookie there.

309
00:11:06,420 --> 00:11:06,820
金粉闪闪啊
Glitter!

310
00:11:07,156 --> 00:11:10,140
估计这牙仙子从来不用扫地吧
I guess the tooth fairy doesn't have to worry about vacuuming.

311
00:11:10,140 --> 00:11:14,140
亲爱的莉莉 我来信是因为我犯了错
See, "Dear Lily, I'm writing because I made a mistake"

312
00:11:14,140 --> 00:11:15,700
给了你太多的钱
"and gave you too much money."

313
00:11:15,700 --> 00:11:19,175
请你今晚把那100美元放在枕头下
"Please leave the $100 under your pillow tonight,"

314
00:11:19,740 --> 00:11:21,720
我会给你1美元
"and I'll give you a dollar.

315
00:11:22,420 --> 00:11:23,620
抱歉让你伤心了[咬到你]
Sorry if that bites."

316
00:11:24,160 --> 00:11:25,880
让我看看
Let me see that.

317
00:11:26,940 --> 00:11:28,180
我不识字
I can't read.

318
00:11:29,200 --> 00:11:31,820
听起来她真的很烦恼
Uh, well, it sounds like she's really in a jam.

319
00:11:31,820 --> 00:11:32,961
我觉得 我们必须
And I think we're gonna

320
00:11:32,961 --> 00:11:34,938
把那100美元还给牙仙子
have to give the tooth fairy her $100 back.

321
00:11:35,695 --> 00:11:37,111
不行 我想留着
No! I wanna keep it.

322
00:11:40,318 --> 00:11:41,498
想到要靠她给我们养老
I'm scared that she's gonna be the one

323
00:11:41,498 --> 00:11:43,337
-就觉得好可怕 -是啊
- taking care of us when we're older. - Yeah.

324
00:11:45,560 --> 00:11:46,460
查克·斯通
"Chuck Stone,"

325
00:11:46,460 --> 00:11:49,053
身高6英尺 火眼晶晶坚韧不拔的硬汉
"6-foot, 3-inches of steely eyed determination"

326
00:11:49,400 --> 00:11:51,420
坐在审讯桌前
"sat at the interrogation table."

327
00:11:53,100 --> 00:11:54,840
他的脑海一片空白
"His mind was a blank..."

328
00:11:55,500 --> 00:11:58,120
空空如也
"A complete blank.

329
00:11:59,140 --> 00:12:02,340
他一件实在的事情都想不出来
"He literally could not think of one single, solitary thing.

330
00:12:02,760 --> 00:12:03,900
这时 他发现了一块污渍
"Then he noticed a spot."

331
00:12:05,540 --> 00:12:07,860
像是早餐时滴落的糖浆
"It looked like syrup left over from breakfast..."

332
00:12:08,840 --> 00:12:10,880
这让他想起来 该吃午饭了
"Which made him realize it was lunchtime."

333
00:12:10,880 --> 00:12:12,862
他吃了块培根生菜番茄三明治
"A bacon, lettuce, and tomato, sandwich--"

334
00:12:12,862 --> 00:12:15,060
查克·斯通管它叫"培生番"
"Or B.L.T, as Chuck Stone called it--

335
00:12:15,060 --> 00:12:16,700
这顿饭正和他胃口
"would really hit the spot."

336
00:12:17,280 --> 00:12:19,880
查克发现 这美味的诀窍在于蛋黄酱
"The secret, chuck realized, was real mayonnaise..."

337
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:22,860
而不是他老婆平时买给儿子的健康食品
"Not that healthy crap his wife kept buying for their son."

338
00:12:22,940 --> 00:12:23,360
该死的
Damn it!

339
00:12:23,602 --> 00:12:26,972
一大串T到底是什么意思
"I mean, what's the point of t-t-t-t-t-t-t?"

340
00:12:26,972 --> 00:12:29,313
你和我 共饮茶
"Tea for two. Two for tea."

341
00:12:30,120 --> 00:12:31,880
之后写的就更加不堪入目了
It only gets worse from here.

342
00:12:32,780 --> 00:12:34,140
你开什么玩笑
You can't be serious!

343
00:12:34,260 --> 00:12:35,840
格尔·索普是我的死对头
Gil Thorpe is my nemesis!

344
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:37,000
菲尔 我不想打击你
I hate to break it to you, Phil,

345
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:37,900
但你不是蝙蝠侠
but you're not Batman.

346
00:12:38,060 --> 00:12:38,680
相信我
Trust me.

347
00:12:39,100 --> 00:12:41,600
格尔非常阴险 他是利用你来对付我
Gil's a snake and he's found the perfect way to mess with me.

348
00:12:41,780 --> 00:12:44,140
你就从来没想过也许他想雇我是因为
Did it ever occur to you that he was hiring me because of...

349
00:12:44,140 --> 00:12:45,420
不知道 我很能干
I don't know? Me.

350
00:12:45,460 --> 00:12:47,540
你开什么玩笑 你到底是谁的老婆
Are you kidding? What's your last name?!

351
00:12:47,720 --> 00:12:48,480
现在还真难说
Right now?

352
00:12:49,440 --> 00:12:50,520
对不起 克莱尔
I'm sorry, Claire.

353
00:12:50,980 --> 00:12:53,140
我也不想 但我要行使我的否决权
I-I hate to do this, but I have to use my veto.

354
00:12:53,399 --> 00:12:55,780
否决权 你才没有什么否决权
Veto? Oh, you don't get any vetoes.

355
00:12:55,780 --> 00:12:57,040
你总是否决我
You veto me all the time.

356
00:12:57,040 --> 00:12:58,070
因为你的想法都太蠢了
'Cause you have dumb ideas.

357
00:12:58,240 --> 00:12:59,160
你倒是举个例子听听
Name one.

358
00:12:59,480 --> 00:13:00,760
她说了好久
That went on for a while.

359
00:13:01,400 --> 00:13:04,140
还有在浴室里存零食的主意
...And let's not forget shower snacks.

360
00:13:04,560 --> 00:13:07,060
不可能只有我会洗澡洗得肚子饿
I can't be the only one who gets hungry in there!

361
00:13:12,880 --> 00:13:14,660
杰 我妈说你在写书
Hey, Jay. My mom said you were writing a book.

362
00:13:14,660 --> 00:13:15,520
真是帅呆了啊
That's fantastic.

363
00:13:16,680 --> 00:13:18,780
顺便提一句 今天的职业日有点奇怪
By the way, Career Day was a little weird.

364
00:13:18,940 --> 00:13:21,000
我觉得克莱尔最近心情不好
I think Claire's going through some pretty dark stuff,

365
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:22,520
-你也许该去关心一下 -别闲聊了
- and you might want to check... - Enough chitchat.

366
00:13:22,520 --> 00:13:24,257
我正想办法让我的主角走出困境呢
I've gotta get a character out of a bind.

367
00:13:24,493 --> 00:13:25,680
他怎么了
Ooh. What did he do?

368
00:13:25,680 --> 00:13:27,440
他跟他老婆说 他能写本书
He told his wife he could write a book.

369
00:13:27,820 --> 00:13:30,280
别放弃 杰 自我怀疑是个必经过程
Don't give up, Jay. Self-doubt is part of the process.

370
00:13:30,700 --> 00:13:31,580
如果你不自我批判
You can't be a good writer

371
00:13:31,580 --> 00:13:33,160
你就成不了一个好作家
without being critical of your own work.

372
00:13:36,800 --> 00:13:37,200
怎么了
What?

373
00:13:38,040 --> 00:13:39,920
我实在想不出好话来鼓励你
I'm racking my brain for a compliment here.

374
00:13:40,120 --> 00:13:41,220
我知道 写得烂透了
I know. It stinks.

375
00:13:41,420 --> 00:13:43,800
这回要让你妈看笑话了
And your mom's gonna rub it in my face pretty good.

376
00:13:43,980 --> 00:13:46,680
好 查克·斯通为什么要审问这个人
Okay. Why is Chuck Stone interrogating this guy?

377
00:13:46,680 --> 00:13:48,833
他需要知道密码 否则的话
He needs the codes. If he doesn't get 'em,

378
00:13:48,833 --> 00:13:50,580
国际空间站就会
the International Space Station's gonna

379
00:13:50,580 --> 00:13:51,920
在除夕夜坠落在时代广场
crash into Times Square on New Year's Eve.

380
00:13:51,960 --> 00:13:52,860
所以他时间无多了
So he's short of time.

381
00:13:52,860 --> 00:13:54,540
他只剩两分钟 他走投无路了
He's got about two minutes. He's desperate.

382
00:13:54,540 --> 00:13:55,680
这样如何
How about this?

383
00:13:56,420 --> 00:13:58,700
查克·斯通笑了笑 点燃一支烟
"Chuck Stone smiled and lit a cigarette,"

384
00:13:58,700 --> 00:14:01,360
仿佛他还有大把的时间
"as if he had all the time in the world,"

385
00:14:01,360 --> 00:14:03,720
然而其实 地球快要毁灭了
when in fact, the world was about to end."

386
00:14:03,800 --> 00:14:05,280
精彩啊 然后呢然后呢
Holy crap. What happens next?

387
00:14:05,280 --> 00:14:06,566
你让开 我来写
Move over. I'll type.

388
00:14:13,800 --> 00:14:15,700
给我来点咖啡吧 谢谢
Some coffee would be great. Thanks.

389
00:14:19,760 --> 00:14:21,180
抱歉 但我不明白为什么
I'm sorry. I don't understand why

390
00:14:21,180 --> 00:14:22,240
我们不能直接走进去
we don't just go in there,

391
00:14:22,240 --> 00:14:24,040
告诉她我们要把钱拿走 就完事了
we tell her we're taking the money, and that's that.

392
00:14:24,080 --> 00:14:25,520
因为这是个教育孩子的机会
Because this is a teaching moment,

393
00:14:25,520 --> 00:14:27,720
我们得引导她自愿把钱交出来
and we want her to want to give the money back.

394
00:14:27,760 --> 00:14:28,780
我只是非常担心
I'm just really worried

395
00:14:28,780 --> 00:14:30,997
我们要成为过分放纵孩子的家长了
we're becoming those overindulgent parents right now.

396
00:14:31,240 --> 00:14:32,120
别傻了
Don't be silly.

397
00:14:32,560 --> 00:14:33,680
好 牙仙子 你准备好了吗
Okay, you ready, tooth fairy?

398
00:14:33,800 --> 00:14:36,240
-行动吧 -好吧
- Let's do this. - All right.

399
00:14:43,360 --> 00:14:45,740
莉莉 看谁来了
Lily, look who came to say hi!

400
00:14:45,740 --> 00:14:48,860
是我 牙仙子
It's me, the tooth fairy.

401
00:14:48,940 --> 00:14:52,240
我来是想请你帮个忙
And I've come to ask you for a favor!

402
00:14:52,500 --> 00:14:54,580
你真的是牙仙子吗
Are you really the tooth fairy?

403
00:14:54,580 --> 00:14:57,659
是的 看我的翅膀
Oh, yes, I am. Look at my wings!

404
00:14:57,659 --> 00:15:01,100
你会飞吗 我想看你飞
Can you fly? I wanna see you fly.

405
00:15:01,100 --> 00:15:03,740
我现在飞不了 因为...
Well, I can't right now because...

406
00:15:03,740 --> 00:15:05,320
因为...
Well, because--

407
00:15:05,320 --> 00:15:09,200
因为牙仙子太伤心了
Because the tooth fairy's too sad to fly...

408
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:12,800
因为她犯了错 只有你能帮她解决
Because she made a mistake that only you can make better.

409
00:15:12,920 --> 00:15:14,760
又是因为那钱吗
Is this about the money again?

410
00:15:14,760 --> 00:15:16,800
是的 没错
Well, yes, it is.

411
00:15:16,920 --> 00:15:21,300
我还得留着钱给别的小盆友呢
I need enough for all the other children's tooths.

412
00:15:21,300 --> 00:15:22,460
-小朋友 -慢着
- Teeth. - Wait a minute.

413
00:15:22,460 --> 00:15:25,080
你不是牙仙子 你是海莉
You're not the tooth fairy. You're Haley.

414
00:15:25,080 --> 00:15:27,160
不 我是牙仙子
No! I am the tooth fairy!

415
00:15:27,380 --> 00:15:29,320
看 我有仙女金粉
Look! Fairy dust!

416
00:15:29,320 --> 00:15:30,400
金粉又得辛苦我扫地了
And there's that glitter.

417
00:15:30,880 --> 00:15:31,860
你们为什么撒谎
Why did you lie?

418
00:15:31,960 --> 00:15:33,360
你们说过撒谎是不对的
You said lying was wrong.

419
00:15:33,460 --> 00:15:37,320
我们也说过 要帮助遇到困难的人
We also said that when someone is in trouble, you help them.

420
00:15:37,760 --> 00:15:39,500
我怎么知道你们不是在骗我
How do I know you weren't lying?

421
00:15:39,760 --> 00:15:40,680
她太聪明了
She is good.

422
00:15:40,780 --> 00:15:42,080
好吧莉莉 不胡闹了
All right, Lily, this is ridiculous.

423
00:15:42,200 --> 00:15:44,460
牙仙子犯了个错
All right, the tooth fairy has made a mistake.

424
00:15:44,460 --> 00:15:46,540
你必须把那100美元放到枕头下
You need to put the $100 under the pillow,

425
00:15:46,540 --> 00:15:47,460
就这样 没得商量
and that is the end of the story.

426
00:15:47,520 --> 00:15:49,940
因为你觉得这样做是对的
Because you believe it's the right thing to do...

427
00:15:49,940 --> 00:15:50,783
-没错 -对吧
- Yes. - Don't you?

428
00:15:51,018 --> 00:15:52,723
可是我想买滑板车
But I wanna buy a scooter.

429
00:15:52,723 --> 00:15:54,124
换我也会这么做
Oh. That's what I'd do.

430
00:15:55,300 --> 00:15:55,960
我是说
I mean...

431
00:15:56,360 --> 00:15:58,800
管他圣诞老人怎么想呢
Who cares what Santa thinks, right?

432
00:15:59,840 --> 00:16:00,400
圣诞老人
Santa?

433
00:16:01,040 --> 00:16:02,660
对啊 他全都看在眼里
Well, he sees everything,

434
00:16:03,100 --> 00:16:05,500
这事恐怕会让他把你放进坏孩子名单
And this'll probably put you on the "Naughty" list.

435
00:16:05,500 --> 00:16:08,240
可你根本不必每年等他来给你送礼物
But who needs presents every year?

436
00:16:08,240 --> 00:16:10,553
因为你自己都有100美元了
You've got a hundred dollars.

437
00:16:10,840 --> 00:16:13,040
你可以骑着滑板车在空空的圣诞树下
You can ride around that empty christmas tree

438
00:16:13,040 --> 00:16:14,140
晃悠到变成老太太为止
until you're an old lady.

439
00:16:14,900 --> 00:16:16,920
可以给我些时间考虑下吗
Can I have some time to think about it?

440
00:16:17,040 --> 00:16:19,040
-你不需要时间 -当然可以 宝贝
- You don't need any... - Of course, sweetie.

441
00:16:19,040 --> 00:16:20,145
好的
Yeah. Okay.

442
00:16:23,274 --> 00:16:25,360
海莉 这招太高了
Haley? Okay, that was brilliant.

443
00:16:25,360 --> 00:16:27,360
多谢 这身行头可以借我吗
Thanks. Oh, also, can I borrow this?

444
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:29,100
-为什么 -我还是不说的好
- Why? - I'd rather not say.

445
00:16:30,120 --> 00:16:32,120
我戴上假发后
You know, after I put on the wig,

446
00:16:32,580 --> 00:16:34,860
可以感觉到融入角色了
I just... I felt like the character.

447
00:16:35,300 --> 00:16:35,860
等等
Hang on.

448
00:16:35,860 --> 00:16:37,220
侬好哇
Yell-o?

449
00:16:37,220 --> 00:16:39,960
问一下 这是真正的菲尔还是视频菲尔
Quick question. Am I talking to live Phil or video Phil?

450
00:16:40,640 --> 00:16:41,560
你想干嘛 格尔
What do you want, Gil?

451
00:16:41,560 --> 00:16:43,840
只想确定下你不介意你老婆叫我"大老板"
I just wanna make sure it's okay that your wife calls me "Boss."

452
00:16:44,061 --> 00:16:46,296
-再见 -慢着 别挂
- Good-bye. - Oh, hold on! Hold on!

453
00:16:46,296 --> 00:16:47,680
我逗你玩儿呢
I'm just messing with ya.

454
00:16:47,880 --> 00:16:48,520
但我的确认为
Although I do think

455
00:16:48,520 --> 00:16:49,820
你老婆会很享受在我"下面"办事
your wife's gonna enjoy being under me.

456
00:16:49,940 --> 00:16:51,260
我儿子在车里
My son is in the car.

457
00:16:51,380 --> 00:16:53,220
大明星 还好吗
Hey, superstar! What's up?

458
00:16:53,220 --> 00:16:55,340
听着 任何时候你想来海边别墅
Listen, any time you wanna swing by the beach house,

459
00:16:55,340 --> 00:16:57,520
我都很乐意教你如何扔橄榄回旋球
I'll be glad to show you how to throw a tight spiral

460
00:16:57,520 --> 00:16:59,160
就像我当年在德州理工那样 好耶
like I did at Texas Tech. Booyah!

461
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:01,500
-汤米 -他已经会扔了
- Tommy! - He already knows how to throw.

462
00:17:01,680 --> 00:17:04,140
-我的同志舅夫小卡教我了 -让我来
- Yeah, my gay uncle Cam taught me. - I-I got this.

463
00:17:04,280 --> 00:17:06,640
这是我们的恩怨 不能把家人扯进来
This was between us. You don't bring family into it.

464
00:17:06,640 --> 00:17:08,240
让克莱尔空欢喜一场 你真是卑鄙
Low blow getting Claire's hopes up.

465
00:17:08,340 --> 00:17:09,580
我没有让她空欢喜一场
Hey, I'm not getting her hopes up.

466
00:17:09,580 --> 00:17:11,840
这是有着真正好处的真正工作
This is a real job with real bennies--

467
00:17:11,840 --> 00:17:12,880
其中一项好处就是
One of which is

468
00:17:12,880 --> 00:17:14,520
任何时候她俯身在我桌前
I get to tell you what I'm thinking

469
00:17:14,520 --> 00:17:16,300
我都可以告诉你我的想法
whenever she leans over my desk!

470
00:17:17,360 --> 00:17:19,840
这下我真是要开心死了
Oh, I'm gonna have so much fun with this!

471
00:17:19,840 --> 00:17:21,635
回见了 小邓邓
Later, Dunph-bags!

472
00:17:22,720 --> 00:17:23,580
真是个混蛋
What a jerk.

473
00:17:23,780 --> 00:17:24,780
知道吗 得在你妈妈
You know what? We're gonna tell your mom

474
00:17:24,780 --> 00:17:26,320
答应与他合作前 告诉她
before she goes into business with this guy.

475
00:17:26,320 --> 00:17:29,305
他真是"格"犹如"索普在背"的烦人精
He's Gil-ty of being a Thorpe in my side.

476
00:17:30,260 --> 00:17:31,140
太刻意了
Trying too hard.

477
00:17:31,540 --> 00:17:32,020
是的
Yeah.

478
00:17:34,060 --> 00:17:34,540
我回来了
Hello!

479
00:17:35,500 --> 00:17:35,960
闪一边去
Move!

480
00:17:37,040 --> 00:17:37,740
你没事
You're fine.

481
00:17:39,760 --> 00:17:40,320
怎么样
So?

482
00:17:41,260 --> 00:17:43,480
第一天写作如何啊
How was your first day of writing?

483
00:17:43,600 --> 00:17:45,500
歌洛莉亚 安静 让我写完最后一句
Gloria, shh! Let me finish one thought.

484
00:17:46,920 --> 00:17:47,680
好了
Got it.

485
00:17:48,520 --> 00:17:50,300
你真的写出了东西吗
So you actually wrote something?

486
00:17:50,320 --> 00:17:51,600
开始比较不顺
Well, it was slow going at first,

487
00:17:51,600 --> 00:17:53,120
然后就文思如泉涌了
but then the juices started flowing.

488
00:17:53,760 --> 00:17:54,860
-我能看看吗 -当然
- May I? - Sure.

489
00:17:54,860 --> 00:17:57,000
如果有帮助的话 把主角意淫成汤姆·贝伦杰
Uh, if it helps, picture Tom Berenger.

490
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:58,340
我总是意淫着别人
I always do.

491
00:18:03,240 --> 00:18:03,580
怎么了
What?

492
00:18:03,580 --> 00:18:03,860
只是
Well, it's just this...

493
00:18:03,860 --> 00:18:07,560
第一句有点长啊
This first sentence is a bit long.

494
00:18:07,760 --> 00:18:09,000
是长还是生动形象
Long or dynamic?

495
00:18:09,271 --> 00:18:12,920
又长又令人迷惑 我分不清是谁在说话
No, long and confusing. I can't tell who's talking.

496
00:18:12,920 --> 00:18:14,920
也许这是模仿《战争迷雾》
Maybe that's just to mimic The Fog of Battle.

497
00:18:15,860 --> 00:18:16,120
好吧
Okay.

498
00:18:18,660 --> 00:18:19,440
又怎么了
What now?

499
00:18:19,944 --> 00:18:23,740
只是 1965年时没有手机
Just... There were no cell phones in 1965.

500
00:18:23,740 --> 00:18:25,120
那是个错误 我会改的
That's a mistake. I'm changing that.

501
00:18:25,180 --> 00:18:27,400
不能改 结尾又会出现
You can't change that. It comes back in the end...

502
00:18:27,400 --> 00:18:28,500
我猜想的
I-I presume.

503
00:18:28,500 --> 00:18:30,060
重点是 我可以写作
The point is, I can write.

504
00:18:30,180 --> 00:18:31,680
我可能不会以此为业
I probably won't pursue it,

505
00:18:31,680 --> 00:18:33,240
但这是可行的职业选择
but it's a viable career option.

506
00:18:33,420 --> 00:18:36,200
中情局有着各种顶级机密的高科技
The CIA had all sorts of top-secret technology.

507
00:18:36,380 --> 00:18:38,000
你怎么知道他们当时没有手机
Who's to say they didn't have cell phones?

508
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:39,100
曼尼 算了
Manny, let it go.

509
00:18:39,626 --> 00:18:41,440
这个查克·斯通
And this Chuck Stone--

510
00:18:41,440 --> 00:18:43,760
似乎不太擅长他的工作啊
He doesn't seem very good at his job.

511
00:18:43,760 --> 00:18:46,420
他有缺点 这样角色才会有趣
He's flawed. That's what makes the character interesting.

512
00:18:46,420 --> 00:18:48,800
如果你要完美的 用机器人好了
If you want someone perfect, put in a robot.

513
00:18:49,400 --> 00:18:50,240
机器人
A robot!

514
00:18:50,480 --> 00:18:51,600
我喜欢机器人
I like a robot.

515
00:18:51,740 --> 00:18:54,080
不 我的故事中不能有机器人
No! You're not putting a robot in my story!

516
00:18:54,460 --> 00:18:56,120
没错 这是我写的
That's right, my story.

517
00:18:58,800 --> 00:19:00,360
你肯定开心死了
You must be very happy.

518
00:19:00,660 --> 00:19:03,480
我本该开心的 但生活妨碍了我开心
I would be, but life got in the way.

519
00:19:08,500 --> 00:19:09,280
你在做什么
What are you doing?

520
00:19:09,420 --> 00:19:10,880
找出了我以前的公文包
Oh, I just got out my old briefcase.

521
00:19:10,880 --> 00:19:12,660
还是可以重返职场的
It's still capable of doing the job,

522
00:19:13,160 --> 00:19:14,020
和我一样
Just like me.

523
00:19:14,120 --> 00:19:15,540
克莱尔 有些事你得知道
Claire, you have to understand something.

524
00:19:15,540 --> 00:19:16,840
有些事你得知道
You have to understand something.

525
00:19:16,840 --> 00:19:18,800
我整天都沉浸在幸福之中
I walked around all day on cloud nine

526
00:19:18,800 --> 00:19:20,400
因为有人赏识我的价值
because somebody valued me.

527
00:19:20,440 --> 00:19:22,740
我赏识你的价值 我们都如此
I value you. We all value you.

528
00:19:22,760 --> 00:19:24,480
你们当然赏识
No, of course you do,

529
00:19:24,480 --> 00:19:27,200
因为我做饭 打扫 收拾脏内衣
Because I cook and I clean and I pick up dirty underwear.

530
00:19:27,320 --> 00:19:28,840
亲爱的 这个不一样
No, honey, it's different than that.

531
00:19:28,840 --> 00:19:30,900
我已经做旁观者很多年了
I have been on the sidelines for so long,

532
00:19:31,080 --> 00:19:32,780
我不知道是否还会有人认为
I didn't know if anybody would ever think

533
00:19:32,780 --> 00:19:33,800
我有能力重新工作
I have what it takes again.

534
00:19:34,240 --> 00:19:36,520
我知道格尔不是什么好人
I know Gil's not the greatest guy,

535
00:19:36,520 --> 00:19:38,460
但这很重要 我想
But this is important. And I think--

536
00:19:38,460 --> 00:19:39,720
我想你应该接受这份工作
I think you should take the job.

537
00:19:40,400 --> 00:19:41,180
但是 爸
But, dad...

538
00:19:41,180 --> 00:19:42,720
不 卢克 你妈说得对
No, Luke. She's right.

539
00:19:43,706 --> 00:19:45,463
她会非常出色的
Your mom's gonna be amazing at this.

540
00:19:50,100 --> 00:19:52,340
-我收回否决权 -你从未有过否决权
- I retract my veto. - You never had a veto.

541
00:19:52,420 --> 00:19:54,460
-我有 -你没有 我告诉你为什么
- Yes, I did. - No, you didn't, and I'll tell you why.

542
00:19:54,780 --> 00:19:56,480
她又说了好久
And that went on for a while.

543
00:19:57,200 --> 00:19:59,540
最后 这番对话就会发生在
...And lastly, this whole conversation would be happening

544
00:19:59,540 --> 00:20:01,440
-圆顶帐篷中 -那是完美的结构
- in a yurt. - It's the perfect structure.

545
00:20:01,580 --> 00:20:03,640
我得把旧西装里的垫肩都拿掉
I have to go take the shoulder pads out of all my old suits!

546
00:20:05,511 --> 00:20:07,107
你知道他会继续取笑你吧
You know he's gonna keep teasing you.

547
00:20:07,107 --> 00:20:09,814
只要你妈妈开心 我能承受几个电话
If it makes your mom happy, I can handle a few phone calls.

548
00:20:12,620 --> 00:20:13,420
还有短信
And texts.

549
00:20:14,240 --> 00:20:16,320
-说了什么 -没什么我不能承受的
- What does it say? - Nothing I can't handle.

550
00:20:18,540 --> 00:20:20,660
"我们都在编织着谎言之网
"We all weave a web of lies."

551
00:20:23,080 --> 00:20:25,980
有些谎言 是为了帮助所爱的人
"Some we tell to try to help the ones we love."

552
00:20:31,160 --> 00:20:32,820
有些谎言 是为了欺骗自己"
"Some we tell to try to fool ourselves."

553
00:20:35,580 --> 00:20:37,220
"有些谎言 是因为
"And some we tell because,

554
00:20:37,220 --> 00:20:38,380
当子弹用尽
when you're out of bullets

555
00:20:38,380 --> 00:20:40,620
凝视着冲锋枪的枪管时
and staring down the barrel of a kalashnikov,

556
00:20:41,160 --> 00:20:43,300
剩下的武器只有 诡计"
the only weapon you've got left is guile."

557
00:20:44,080 --> 00:20:46,380
你妈妈太不识货了 这棒极了
She's nuts. That's fantastic.

558
00:20:50,780 --> 00:20:52,340
孩子们 快过来
Okay, guys, bring it in!

559
00:20:52,800 --> 00:20:54,880
在妈妈回家前 我们要把家里收拾干净
Let's get this place shipshape before she gets home.

560
00:20:55,020 --> 00:20:56,360
我肯定她第一天上班很辛苦
I'm sure she had a big first day.

561
00:20:56,520 --> 00:20:58,020
海莉 你负责洗衣服
Haley, I'm putting you on laundry.

562
00:20:58,240 --> 00:20:59,460
艾丽克斯 收拾厨房与吸尘
Alex, kitchen and vacuum.

563
00:20:59,580 --> 00:21:00,760
卢克 你清洁厕所
Luke, you're cleaning the bathroom.

564
00:21:01,060 --> 00:21:01,840
为什么是我
Why me?

565
00:21:01,940 --> 00:21:02,980
因为弄脏的人总是你
Because you always mess it up.

566
00:21:02,980 --> 00:21:04,800
你为什么不能尿在马桶里呢
Yeah, why can't you pee straight?

567
00:21:04,920 --> 00:21:06,980
站得那么远 我已经很不错了
Hey, I'm doing a great job from that far back.

568
00:21:07,100 --> 00:21:09,080
好了孩子们 邓菲队数到三加油
Okay, guys, team Dunphy on three.

569
00:21:09,320 --> 00:21:11,980
一 二 对了 有许多事要做
One, two--that's right, we got a lot to do!

570
00:21:13,440 --> 00:21:15,160
亲爱的 你怎么这么早就回来了
Honey, what are you doing home so early?

571
00:21:15,280 --> 00:21:17,660
我辞职了 那家伙是头彻头彻尾的猪
I quit. That man is a complete pig.

572
00:21:17,720 --> 00:21:19,220
他把我当仆人一样使唤
He treated me like a servant

573
00:21:19,220 --> 00:21:20,800
完全不尊重我
and showed me absolutely no respect.

574
00:21:20,800 --> 00:21:22,760
太遗憾了 你不该受到那样的待遇
I'm so sorry. You deserve better than that.

575
00:21:22,900 --> 00:21:23,480
的确是
I do.

576
00:21:24,800 --> 00:21:25,920
晚饭吃什么
So what's for dinner?

577
00:21:27,480 --> 00:21:29,640
你是不是听错了 我是说你晚饭想吃什么
I feel like you heard me wrong. I said, what's for dinner?

578
00:21:29,640 --> 00:21:30,500
我听得很清楚
I heard you!
